WEBVTT

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.680
Soichiro!

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.580
Don't scare me like that!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.510
Otonashi speaking.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.420
Oh, hello.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.260
What? Yes, I have a vacancy.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.660
What? Right now?

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:27.920
But--

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.040
Hello? Hello?

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.170
Sir!

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.010
Sir!

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.560
Isn't this yours?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.570
Oh, thank you.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.260
If you're going to Maison Ikkoku,
you're heading in the wrong way.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.950
Am I? Thank you.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.220
Looks like it's going to rain.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.820
Well, then.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.070
A new tenant?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.190
Yes.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.660
What's the person like?

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.570
I don't know.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.000
You don't?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.290
It was very sudden.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.700
Whatever. We gotta
have a welcome party.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.250
Godai! You here, Godai?

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.830
W-Wait, Mrs. Ichinose!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.640
Godai!

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.450
Rain.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.390
Oh, no! The laundry!

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.760
Godai!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.530
-Get some munchies, too.
-I know.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.200
And stop at Chachamaru
and tell Akemi that--

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.510
Never mind! I'll just call her!

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.530
-Where is he?
-I don't know.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.750
His things have arrived.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.830
Maybe he ran away.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.010
From what?

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.840
It's odd that he hasn't called.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.420
We got psyched for nothing.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.890
Too bad.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.090
We hadn't had
a new face since Godai.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.520
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.510
-I'm going to bed.
-Me, too.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.700
-Good night.
-Good night.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.070
Um...

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.820
You'll catch a cold.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.680
You haven't had dinner, have you?

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.750
No.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.620
Good morning.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:40.380
Yes?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.860
I'm Mitsukoshi Zenzaburo
your new tenant.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.000
He got delayed because of the rain?

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.940
That's what he said.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.090
I wonder where he was all night?

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.370
I don't know.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:04.710
Ms. Otonashi, I heard
through the grape vine...

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.120
that you have a new tenant.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:14.970
Don't worry. He won't be
a rival to you in any way.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.260
W-What are you talking about?
A rival?

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:22.920
Oh, really? Not that I care.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.220
He's pretty concerned.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.700
Is Mr. Mitsukoshi a tennis player?

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.070
Just one cardboard box?

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.180
That's all he moved in with.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.990
That seems odd.
I'm curious to meet him.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.280
Why?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.220
Why? Because if he
stays at Maison Ikkoku...

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.220
and you stay at Maison Ikkoku
for a long time...

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.000
and if you and l--

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:06.760
What?

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.240
Oh, hello again.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:17.050
-Him?
-Yup.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.130
Cheers!

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.210
I'm so happy.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.080
It's great to have another
person at Maison Ikkoku!

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.530
Drink up!

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.770
We'll take care of you
if you pass out.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.670
Thank you, but--

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.680
C'mon! Drink up!

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.780
Go ahead. Down it!

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.600
If you don't listen to them,
you're asking for trouble.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.910
Whaddaya mean?

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.810
Your sleeves seem a bit long.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.920
Yes, but the hem is too short.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.250
You must really love it
since you've held on to it.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.360
Don't tell me your late wife
handmade it for you.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.200
You're right, actually.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:19.100
I'm so sorry.
I was just trying to be funny.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:21.550
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:23.550
It's all in the past.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.390
Mrs. Ichinose
how about your usual dance?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.820
Oh, yeah.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.650
You haven't had a drop yet.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.450
How about you, Manager?

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.030
Sure.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.570
Maybe I'll let loose tonight.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.830
When this lady lets loose,
she becomes rather scary.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.310
What do you mean?

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.050
Isn't that right, Godai?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.410
W-Why are you asking me?

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.570
Who cares. Let's drink.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.060
Let the party begin!

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.970
Is this what you want? Hold on.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.690
Soichiro, no!

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.610
I'm sorry he got your pants dirty.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.320
No problem.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.710
Say, I have some sweet rolls.
Would you like one?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:51.270
A sweet roll.  I wanted a dessert, and this
is the closest I could get.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.320
No pastries?

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.200
They told me they
didn't have any.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.230
I see.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.000
Please. I don't have
much of an appetite.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.970
Alcohol doesn't agree with me.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:12.390
They all seem like nice people.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.400
I'm glad the weather
was nice today.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:30.310
Oh, I have some milk, too.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.150
I've been lazy about that.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.850
Let me fix that for you.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.060
For sharing this bread.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.290
You don't have to do that.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.980
I'd like to.
My dog got your pants dirty.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.620
What're you doing here?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:12.420
What?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.680
He reminds me of him.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.950
Not in any partiular way...

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.430
but just in general.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.620
Like whom?

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.270
Soichiro.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:20.430
If you don't get rid
of athlete's foot now...

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:23.590
it's a real pain when
it gets warmer.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:26.560
Yes, well...

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.250
You're--

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.010
Yotsuya.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.680
Thank you.
Yotsuya Kikuchiyo...

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:38.680
No, it's written like "Kikuchiyo,"
but it's read "Tamezo."

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.450
People call me
"Kind-hearted Tame-san."

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.400
Heading home from work?

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.220
Well, yes.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:56.200
It's hard to work when
it's this nice outside.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.170
You think so, too?

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.060
Yes.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.090
Would you like one?

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.950
Have you been at
Maison Ikkoku long, Yotsuya?

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:16.890
I can't even remember
when I moved in.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.160
Have you ever
thought of moving out?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.890
What about you?

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:22.820
Huh?

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:29.720
Of all these apartment buildings,
why did you choose Maison Ikkoku?

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:34.240
Well...

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.910
it's the way it smells.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:39.920
What?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.990
It smells like the warmth of spring.
I was drawn to it.

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:58.450
See you.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.140
Mr. Mitsukoshi!

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:05.770
Oh, hello.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.640
Were you with Yotsuya?

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:11.620
Yes, he suggested we have
some soba noodles.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.750
Yotsuya treated you?

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.550
Huh? No.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.340
I knew it.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.160
Is there a supermarket near here?

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.420
Shopping?

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.120
Yes. I need
a small pot and a kettle.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.430
Well, then you're probably better off
at the store by the station.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.400
Shall we run for it?

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:34.410
Sure.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.970
I think that was
the manager and--.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.260
C'mon, Godai. We're gonna start.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:56.520
I'll be right there.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.950
Hey!

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.630
Oh, you spilled.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:02.900
Sorry!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:04.640
Oh, Mrs. Ichinose.

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:07.720
It's okay.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:10.770
It's going to stain.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:14.430
You're such a
"thoughful wife"-type, Manager.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:17.750
She's not like you, Akemi.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:18.910
Whaddaya mean?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.250
Why're you just
standing there, Godai?

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:23.550
N-No reason.

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.420
Let's drink!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.020
Why're you so gung ho?

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.260
Never mind. Beer, please.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.420
You wait.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:37.960
Let the party begin!

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.150
Why the long face?
It's not like you.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:03.590
Leave me alone.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.620
Did something happen between
you and Ms. Otonashi?

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:07.970
No.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:10.690
You're no fun.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:14.270
Oh, by the way, Godai.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:16.900
Yes?

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.510
How's...

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:22.540
How's that new tenant guy?

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:24.540
What do you mean?

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.940
Well, you know.

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:30.520
He's a nice man.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.780
Wait!

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.240
Good evening.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:12.890
Um...

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:13.820
Yes?

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:19.770
N-Never mind.

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.300
It's strange.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:27.270
People at Maison Ikkoku
seem like family to me.

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:31.800
Not one of you questioned
my background...

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:36.040
and you treat me like
I've always lived there.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:39.340
It's hard to describe.
It's strange.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.850
It makes me very happy, but--

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:42.640
"But"?

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.640
Hello, Soichiro.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.030
Sorry. I have
nothing for you today.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.560
You were together?

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.090
We ran into each other.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:55.900
Wasn't it cold?
I made some sweet sake.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:56.700
See what I mean?

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:58.370
Yes, I do.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.400
What is it?

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.710
How about some sweet sake?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:02.400
Sure.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.340
Come with me. I can't guarantee
it'll be good, though.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.400
If you made it, it must be good.

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.260
What? He resembles him?

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.990
She said he reminds her of him.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.770
I was debating whether
or not to tell you.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.940
Maybe she thought so all along.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:08.980
Maybe he'll be
a bigger rival than Mitaka.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:09.870
Please.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:15.250
If she sees Soichiro in him
then you have no chance.

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:19.950
Well, wait and see what happens
before you do anything drastic.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:22.990
What're you two doing?

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.960
Sunning. Wanna join us?

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:40.740
Going out, Mr. Mitsukoshi?
Bye! Have a nice day!

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:57.110
And when he turned on the fan
the chopped up roach came flying.

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.880
and it went right into his nose.

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:02.760
And then when he screamed
it flew out of his mouth!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:04.660
Isn't that funny?

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.190
Godai?

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:09.160
What's the matter?

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:12.510
Sorry. I was just thinking.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:13.800
Thinking?

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.370
Yeah.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.240
I feel sorry for you.

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:23.340
I guess that rumor is true.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:24.720
Rumor?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.390
Ms. Otonashi seems very lively.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:37.230
You think so, too?

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.430
What do you mean,
do I think so, too?

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.470
What're you so upset about?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:47.270
Tell me the truth.
Is that rumor true?

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:48.800
Rumor?

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:51.400
Where'd you hear that?

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:54.480
Don't you know?
Everyone's talking about it.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.340
Who's everyone?

00:21:56.550 --> 00:21:59.340
You know, like our customers.

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:02.120
But if you don't know
anything about it...

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:04.460
then it must just be a rumor.

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:12.520
A-Akemi? Where're you going?
What about work?

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:17.160
Akemi.

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:22.600
Manager!

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:24.680
I just heard something disturbing.

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:26.910
So did we.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.140
It's not true, is it?

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:30.520
What did you hear, Akemi?

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:33.110
That Maison Ikkoku
will be torn down.

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:35.880
So we all heard the same rumor.

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:37.350
What about Mitaka?

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:40.590
He just made his up in his head.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:41.620
What?

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:43.800
That Manager's gonna remarry.

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.890
That's not true.

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:47.300
Not true at all.

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:49.890
Mitaka tends to
jump to conclusions.

00:22:50.610 --> 00:22:51.980
But it's strange.

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:54.160
None of us tenants has heard
anything about it.

00:22:54.880 --> 00:22:56.050
What about Yotsuya?

00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:57.780
I haven't seen him yet today.

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.650
Maybe that's Yotsuya.

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:09.020
How 'bout some tea?

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:10.290
Let's drink instead.

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:11.490
Sounds great.

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.850
Hello, Mr. Mitsukoshi.

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:16.530
Looks like rain again.

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:18.880
Godai, want some beer?

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:21.440
No thanks.

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:51.180
W-What?!

00:23:51.250 --> 00:23:53.450
Calm down, Mrs. Ichinose.

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:56.750
B-But didn't Kozue
see Mr. Mitsukoshi at--

00:23:57.020 --> 00:24:00.930
Next: "Even Yotsuya is Shocked!
The Day Maison Ikkoku Disappears"

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:03.430
I'm the only one who was waiting.

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:06.160
Was I not?
